ellation, assistance and wake: Touch waking attract also activated Play\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"mouse, keyboard aiming, one bolt and native pause\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"maxOwnedBolts\": 1,\n      \"movementCells\": 2.599999999999998,\n      \"music\": 0.1\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"keyboard-only menus and native rebinding\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"rebound\": \"KeyF\",\n      \"restored\": \"Space\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"controller menus, twin sticks, symbols and unplug\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"controller\": \"standard-mapped DualSense stub\",\n      \"glyphs\": \"xbox\",\n      \"disconnect\": \"paused\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"simultaneous couch seats and input ownership\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"actors\": 2,\n      \"mode\": \"simultaneous two-keyboard couch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"10-second attract, loop, save isolation and consumed wake\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"thresholdSeconds\": 10,\n      \"showcaseSeconds\": 85,\n      \"wakes\": [\n        \"keyboard\",\n        \"mouse\"\n      ],\n      \"storageUnchanged\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"controller attract wake and drift policy\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"wakes\": [\n        \"controller\"\n      ],\n      \"deadZoneDriftIgnored\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"developer single-step, live slider, reset and finale\",\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"detail\": \"Single-step did not mark the run Practice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"corrupt and blocked persistence keep the game playable\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"storage\": [\n        \"corrupt JSON\",\n        \"blocked read/write\"\n      ],\n      \"playable\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"full normal campaign through commands, results, credits and replay\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"phase\": \"victory\",\n      \"practice\": false,\n      \"stats\": {\n        \"kills\": 110,\n        \"shots\": 173,\n        \"bells\": 10,\n        \"portals\": 1,\n        \"cloaked\": 25050,\n        \"familiars\": 6,\n        \"escaped\": 0,\n        \"wizardHits\": 5,\n        \"rooms\": 6,\n        \"damage\": 3,\n        \"activeSeconds\": 252.3416666666015\n      },\n      \"room\": 5,\n      \"time\": 252.3416666666015,\n      \"score\": 40500\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"touch multitouch, cancellation, assistance and wake\",\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"detail\": \"Touch waking attract also activated Play\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"WebKit phone touch menus and gameplay\",\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"browser\": \"26.6\",\n      \"device\": \"iPhone13 profile\",\n      \"limitations\": \"Emulation, not a physical iOS Safari device\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hardware\": \"No physical controller, phone, second player or human listening; stubs and browser profiles used.\"\n}\n252:- `game.screen.resize()`: fit the buffer to the canvas again (on window resize; after changing sizing options, setOptions does it)\n254:- `game.screen.setScale(v)`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' | 'fill' | 'auto' (see scale)\n258:- `game.screen.buf`: the low-resolution buffer the game draws into (W + 2 by H + 2 pixels; null when headless, a stand-in when a headless game draws: o.draw)\n262:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.fil [... omitted end of long line]\n263:- `game.screen.fx = 0`, `game.screen.fy = 0`: its sub-pixel part (0..1, applied when presenting)\n265:- `game.screen.listeners = []` †: functions called after every resize\n267:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the la [... omitted end of long line]\n271:- `new E.Input(screen, map, signal) → input`: signal: an AbortSignal that removes every listener this adds (game.dispose()). A screen without a canvas (headless) gets no DOM listeners: input comes fro [... omitted end of long line]\n277:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n280:- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's le [... omitted end of long line]\n283:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, [... omitted end of long line]\n290:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a [... omitted end of long line]\n318:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size the [... omitted end of long line]\n321:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. E [... omitted end of long line]\n355:- `input.zones = null` †: areas of the screen a finger holds an action down in, [{ x0, y0, x1, y1, act }] (fractions of the canvas, 0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's tw [... omitted end of long line]\n384:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n459:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause [... omitted end of long line]\n463:- `new E.Game({ headless })`: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default): scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and inpu [... omitted end of long line]\n518:- `game.upright`: true while the game's screen (r.W x r.H) is upright, taller than 1.3 times its width: a phone held upright, with expand: true (a fixed res keeps its own shape on any phone, so it is  [... omitted end of long line]\n553:- `game.screen`: the low-resolution screen (its W, H, scale and buffer)\n581:- `fullscreen.enter(quiet)`: go full screen. Browsers allow it only from a tap, click or key press: call it from one (a button, the menu, a key's update step). Returns a promise of whether it worked ( [... omitted end of long line]\n794:- `map.chunks` †: the floor baked in squares of 128 screen pixels as the camera comes to them (its colors and the GPU lighting's canvas both), the far ones let go, so a 256 x 256-cell map costs what t [... omitted end of long line]\n985:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game [... omitted end of long line]\n1192:- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n1194:- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n279:        client.wait_for_function(\"__wizard.test.command(0).aim===2\", timeout=3000)\n288:                \"name\": \"actual remote mouse aims relative to seat1 and its click resolves the shared hunter\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '245,258p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md; rg -n 'setOptions\\\\(' vendor/my-3d2dge.js | head -15; sed -n '615,640p' vendor/my-3d2dge.js; sed -n '265,310p' tests/hub_browser.py; rg -n 'touch.*wake|Touch waking|function touch|touch_case' tests/ui_browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '245,258p' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md; rg -n 'setOptions\\\\(' vendor/my-3d2dge.js | head -15; sed -n '615,640p' vendor/my-3d2dge.js; sed -n '265,310p' tests/hub_browser.py; rg -n 'touch.*wake|Touch waking|function touch|touch_case' tests/ui_browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n\n## 4. Screen\n\n- `E.RES: nes, snes, gb, gbc, gba, genesis, md, pce, n64, ps1, wide`: classic console resolutions for new Game({ res: 'snes' }) (width x height in pixels)\n- `game.screen.clear` †: true when the game's bg is null (or 'transparent'): the buffer and the canvas are cleared instead of filled, so a picture under the canvas shows through the game's (a 3D world drawn by engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js)\n- `game.screen.clientToScreen(cx, cy)`: browser client coords -> projected screen pixels (same space as view.p)\n- `game.screen.resize()`: fit the buffer to the canvas again (on window resize; after changing sizing options, setOptions does it)\n- `game.screen.setOptions(o)`: change sizing at runtime, e.g. { minH: 400, maxW: 1080, maxH: 660 } to pull the camera back\n- `game.screen.setScale(v)`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' | 'fill' | 'auto' (see scale)\n- `game.screen.H = 200`, `game.screen.W = 320`: the buffer's size in game pixels\n- `game.screen.OX = 0`, `game.screen.OY = 0`: the letterbox margins on the canvas, in canvas pixels\n- `game.screen.S = 3`: the whole-number scale up to the canvas\n- `game.screen.buf`: the low-resolution buffer the game draws into (W + 2 by H + 2 pixels; null when headless, a stand-in when a headless game draws: o.draw)\n700:  setOptions(o) { Object.assign(this._o, o); this.resize(); }\n2911:    if (ok('res') || ok('expand')) this.screen.setOptions(Object.assign(ok('res') ? { res: s.res } : {}, ok('expand') ? { expand: s.expand } : {}));\n12753:      sc.setOptions({ minW: 1e6, minH: 1e6, maxW: 1e6, maxH: 1e6, portrait: { maxH: 1e6 } }); game.cam.snap = true;\n12754:    } else if (!on && this._res) { const R = this._res; this._res = null; sc.setOptions({ minW: R.minW, minH: R.minH, maxW: R.maxW, maxH: R.maxH, portrait: R.portrait }); game.cam.snap = true; }\n/** the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out) */\nE.VIEW_ORDER = ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown', 'brawler', 'side'];   // 'overhead' is left out: it is for flat games\n/**\n * The classic SNES RPG cheat: in steep ground views (pitch 40-70, like threequarter) characters are drawn from a lower,\n * sprite-like angle so their faces show, at the same height on screen. Humanoid and Blob do this by themselves\n * (option charView: false turns it off for one rig, E.style.charPitch = false for all). E.charView(view) gives that view.\n */\n/** the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89) */\nfunction charView(view) {\n  const P = E.style.charPitch;\n  if (P === false || view.pitchDeg < 40 || view.pitchDeg >= 89) return view;\n  const cp = P || 30, key = view.yawDeg + ':' + view.pitchDeg + ':' + view.scale + ':' + view.zBoost + ':' + cp;\n  let v = _cviews.get(key);\n  // height on screen: kept as the view has it up to 70 degrees; steeper (top-down) views draw upright sprites as tall as three-quarter ones\n  const h = view.pitchDeg <= 70 ? view.zBoost * Math.cos(view.pitchDeg * DEG) : .78;\n  if (!v) { v = new View(view.id, view.label, view.yawDeg, cp, view.scale, h / Math.cos(cp * DEG)); _cviews.set(key, v); }\n  return v;\n}\nconst _cviews = new Map();\nE.charView = charView;\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 4. SCREEN  low-res buffer, whole-number upscale, sub-pixel camera on present\n * ============================================================================= */\n/** classic console resolutions for new Game({ res: 'snes' }) (width x height in pixels) */\nE.RES = { nes: [256, 240], snes: [256, 224], gb: [160, 144], gbc: [160, 144], gba: [240, 160], genesis: [320, 224], md: [320, 224], pce: [256, 224], n64: [320, 240], ps1: [320, 240], wide: [400, 225] };\n            \"__wizard.sim.s.enemies.length===1 && __wizard.sim.s.enemies[0].x>12\",\n            timeout=5000,\n        )\n        client.evaluate(\"__wizard.test.feedCommand(null)\")\n        target = client.evaluate(\"\"\"() => {\n          const g=__wizard.game,S=g.screen,rc=S.canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),p=g.view.p(13.5*16,11.5*16,0);\n          return {x:rc.left+((p[0]-S.ix)*S.S+S.OX-Math.round(S.fx*S.S))/S.dpr,y:rc.top+((p[1]-S.iy)*S.S+S.OY-Math.round(S.fy*S.S))/S.dpr};\n        }\"\"\")\n        iframe_box = client.frame_element().bounding_box()\n        assert iframe_box is not None, \"remote client iframe has no pointer target\"\n        page.mouse.move(\n            iframe_box[\"x\"] + target[\"x\"] + 12, iframe_box[\"y\"] + target[\"y\"] + 3\n        )\n        page.mouse.move(iframe_box[\"x\"] + target[\"x\"], iframe_box[\"y\"] + target[\"y\"])\n        client.wait_for_function(\"__wizard.test.command(0).aim===2\", timeout=3000)\n        page.mouse.down()\n        host.wait_for_function(\n            \"__wizard.sim.s.score>0 && __wizard.sim.s.players[1].stats.kills>0\",\n            timeout=6000,\n        )\n        page.mouse.up()\n        checks.append(\n            {\n                \"name\": \"actual remote mouse aims relative to seat1 and its click resolves the shared hunter\",\n                \"pass\": True,\n            }\n        )\n        client.evaluate(\"__wizard.test.feedCommand({move:-1,aim:2,fire:true})\")\n        host.wait_for_function(\"__wizard.sim.s.players[1]?.boltId\", timeout=5000)\n        page.locator(\"#who\").select_option(\"p1\")\n        page.locator(\"#remove\").click()\n        host.wait_for_function(\n            \"__wizard.sim.s.players.length===1 && __wizard.net.players.length===1\",\n            timeout=5000,\n        )\n        assert host.evaluate(\n            \"__wizard.sim.s.players[0].seat===0 && __wizard.sim.s.bolts.every(b=>b.owner!=='p1')\"\n        ), \"departed actor or bolt survived, or remaining seat was renumbered\"\n        checks.append(\n            {\n                \"name\": \"nonhost departure safely removes its actor, bolt and command ownership\",\n                \"pass\": True,\n            }\n        )\n        tick = host.evaluate(\"__wizard.sim.s.tick\")\n        host.wait_for_function(\n290:                    require(page.evaluate('document.body.dataset.mode===\"title\" && __wizard.ui.screen===\"title\"'),'Touch waking attract also activated Play')\n291:                    return {'device':'Chromium iPhone13 profile','multitouch':True,'cancel':True,'assistance':True,'wake':'touch'}\n293:            check('touch multitouch, cancellation, assistance and wake',touch)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
